# README for grub2-theme-catppuccin

If using grub-mkconfig, select a theme by adding a line to /etc/default/grub
like so:

  GRUB_THEME="/usr/share/grub/themes/catppuccin-mocha-grub-theme/theme.txt"

And then run 'grub-mkconfig -o /boot/grub/grub.cfg' to regenerate the grub
boot menu configuration file.


If NOT using grub-mkconfig, something like the following can be used in
grub.cfg directly:

  insmod font
  if loadfont ($root)/usr/share/grub/themes/catppuccin-mocha-grub-theme/font.pf2; then
    insmod efi_gop
    insmod gfxmenu
    insmod gfxterm
    insmod png
    set gfxmode=auto
    set gfxpayload=keep
    set theme=($root)/usr/share/grub/themes/catppuccin-mocha-grub-theme/theme.txt
    export theme
    terminal_output gfxterm
  fi

Set your $root variable manually or via search, for example:

  search --no-floppy --fs-uuid --set root <UUID of root partition>
